<title>MALAYSIA: Tenaga rises on news of power tariff hike.</title>
<headline>Tenaga rises on news of power tariff hike.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The share price of Malaysia's national power utility Tenaga Nasional Bhd rose in late trading on Wednesday after news that it had been granted higher electricity tariffs.</p>
<p>At 0720GMT, the stock was up 40 cents to 11.30 ringgit.  </p>
<p>Malaysia's Energy, Telecommunications and Posts Minister Leo Moggie told a news conference earlier Wednesday that Tenaga will be allowed to raise power charges by 8.3 percent.</p>
</text>
